      "scene_no": 3,
      "template_id": "concept_diagram",
      "teacher_script": "Like fractions are easy to spot! They are fractions that have the exact same denominator. This means they are parts of a whole that has been divided into the same number of equal pieces. Think of cutting a pizza into 8 slices, then taking 1, 3, or 5 of those slices. Each fraction refers to the same 'size' of slice.",
