    {
      "scene_no": 4,
      "template_id": "concept_diagram",
      "teacher_script": "Unlike fractions, on the other hand, have different denominators. This means the wholes they represent have been divided into a different number of equal parts. Imagine one pizza cut into 4 slices and another into 8 slices. A slice from the first pizza is a different size than a slice from the second, even if both numerators are 1.",
      "template_data": {
