    {
      "scene_no": 6,
      "template_id": "illustrated_scene",
      "teacher_script": "Why does this distinction matter so much? Because when you add or subtract fractions, you're essentially combining or taking away pieces of the same size. With like fractions, it's simple: you just add the numerators. But with unlike fractions, you can't just combine them directly; you must first convert them so they all refer to parts of the same size. This process is finding a common denominator.",
